     "type": "key",
     "style": "methode",
     "title": "Changing units",
     "md": "To change a **big unit to a small unit**, **multiply**: 2.5 km = 2.5 × 1,000 = 2,500 m. To change a **small unit to a big unit**, **divide**: 3,400 g = 3,400 ÷ 1,000 = 3.4 kg. Write the unit in every answer."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "pieges",
     "title": "Common mistakes",
     "md": "- Mixing metres and centimetres in the same sum: change first.\n- Multiplying when you should divide.\n- Writing 1 m = 10 cm (it is 100 cm).\n- Writing kg for litres or the other way round."
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 1",
     "statement": "Change 3 km 250 m into metres.",
     "steps": [
      "3 km = 3 × 1,000 = 3,000 m.",
      "3,000 m + 250 m = 3,250 m."
     ],
     "answer": "3,250 m"
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 2",
     "statement": "A bag holds 2 kg of rice. How many grams are in 4 bags?",
     "steps": [
      "1 kg = 1,000 g, so 2 kg = 2,000 g.",
      "4 × 2,000 = 8,000 g."
     ],
     "answer": "8,000 g (8 kg)"
    }
